LICENCE STRUCTURE
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

This repository is dual-licensed:

  1. CODE  →  Apache License, Version 2.0  (see LICENSE)
  2. DOCS  →  CC BY 4.0                    (see LICENSE-DOCS)

The split is deliberate. Apache-2.0 is the appropriate licence for
reusable software (it includes a patent grant and is compatible with
the mainstream open-source ecosystem). CC BY 4.0 is the standard
licence for prose, slides, and notebook narratives. Creative Commons
themselves recommend against using CC licences for software:

    https://creativecommons.org/faq/#can-i-apply-a-creative-commons-license-to-software

This dual structure was adopted in push #28a (2026-05-08) in response
to an external software-product-maturity audit (INV-030).

